window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-076.json",{"day":76,"title":"A Second Chance to Learn","targetWords":[{"word":"academy","gloss":"学院","context":"The academy opened its evening doors to adults who had left secondary education early.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dean","gloss":"院长","context":"Its dean refused to describe an illiterate learner as a failure.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dictionary","gloss":"词典","context":"Another compiled a dictionary of unfamiliar workplace terms.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"verb","gloss":"动词","context":"The group compared a singular verb with its changed form, then joined ideas using a conjunction.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"semester","gloss":"学期","context":"A certificate would eventually recognize progress, but the semester was designed around everyday confidence rather than the collection of another credential.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"session","gloss":"课","context":"The first session therefore began with practical goals: reading a medicine label, writing an address, or understanding a child's nursery notice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"column","gloss":"专栏","context":"An editorial in a local newspaper became the subject of a seminar, while a short column prompted debate about bus fares.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"secondary","gloss":"中等教育的","context":"The academy opened its evening doors to adults who had left secondary education early.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"index","gloss":"索引","context":"Learners used a directory to locate services and an index to find information in a handbook.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"seminar","gloss":"研讨会","context":"An editorial in a local newspaper became the subject of a seminar, while a short column prompted debate about bus fares.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"thesis","gloss":"论文","context":"Many participants had worked since childhood or cared for relatives, and an unfamiliar alphabet could be as difficult as a university thesis.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"junior","gloss":"年轻的","context":"A junior volunteer prepared a summary so that everyone could return to the main points.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"summary","gloss":"摘要","context":"A junior volunteer prepared a summary so that everyone could return to the main points.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"agenda","gloss":"议程","context":"Their agenda included a visit to a municipal office, where a specimen application helped them prepare their own forms.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"nursery","gloss":"托儿所","context":"The first session therefore began with practical goals: reading a medicine label, writing an address, or understanding a child's nursery notice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pencil","gloss":"铅笔","context":"A volunteer mentor gave each learner a notebook, a pen, and a pencil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"illiterate","gloss":"不会读写的","context":"Its dean refused to describe an illiterate learner as a failure.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"pen","gloss":"钢笔","context":"A volunteer mentor gave each learner a notebook, a pen, and a pencil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"alphabet","gloss":"字母表","context":"Many participants had worked since childhood or cared for relatives, and an unfamiliar alphabet could be as difficult as a university thesis.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"certificate","gloss":"证书","context":"A certificate would eventually recognize progress, but the semester was designed around everyday confidence rather than the collection of another credential.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"kindergarten","gloss":"幼儿园","context":"A kindergarten brochure, a health pamphlet, and a library leaflet supplied genuine reading practice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"sociology","gloss":"社会学","context":"The curriculum included arithmetic and a little sociology: participants investigated why some families could access education more easily than others.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"diploma","gloss":"文凭","context":"A quiz identified what needed more practice, but no diploma promise replaced careful feedback.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"pronoun","gloss":"代词","context":"On the wall, chalk showed how a noun could take a plural ending and how a pronoun could replace it.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"catalog","gloss":"目录","context":"Materials came from the neighborhood rather than a remote academic catalog.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"arithmetic","gloss":"算术","context":"The curriculum included arithmetic and a little sociology: participants investigated why some families could access education more easily than others.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"clause","gloss":"从句","context":"Instead of memorizing an isolated clause, they wrote messages they actually wanted to send.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"editorial","gloss":"社论","context":"An editorial in a local newspaper became the subject of a seminar, while a short column prompted debate about bus fares.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"handwriting","gloss":"笔迹","context":"Handwriting was assessed for readability, not elegance.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"oral","gloss":"口头的","context":"A brief oral discussion allowed participants to explain what they meant before turning the thought into a written sentence, making the page less intimidating.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"credential","gloss":"资格证明","context":"A certificate would eventually recognize progress, but the semester was designed around everyday confidence rather than the collection of another credential.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"mentor","gloss":"导师","context":"A volunteer mentor gave each learner a notebook, a pen, and a pencil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pamphlet","gloss":"小册子","context":"A kindergarten brochure, a health pamphlet, and a library leaflet supplied genuine reading practice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"conjunction","gloss":"连词","context":"The group compared a singular verb with its changed form, then joined ideas using a conjunction.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"paperback","gloss":"平装书","context":"A paperback story introduced the pleasure of reading beyond necessity.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"brochure","gloss":"手册","context":"A kindergarten brochure, a health pamphlet, and a library leaflet supplied genuine reading practice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"directory","gloss":"名录","context":"Learners used a directory to locate services and an index to find information in a handbook.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"quiz","gloss":"小测验","context":"A quiz identified what needed more practice, but no diploma promise replaced careful feedback.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"singular","gloss":"单数的","context":"The group compared a singular verb with its changed form, then joined ideas using a conjunction.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"manuscript","gloss":"手稿","context":"A learner who had once used shorthand at work submitted a handwritten manuscript about her experiences.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"notebook","gloss":"笔记本","context":"A volunteer mentor gave each learner a notebook, a pen, and a pencil.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"preface","gloss":"前言","context":"Its preface explained why the author had chosen simple language.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"leaflet","gloss":"传单","context":"A kindergarten brochure, a health pamphlet, and a library leaflet supplied genuine reading practice.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"noun","gloss":"名词","context":"On the wall, chalk showed how a noun could take a plural ending and how a pronoun could replace it.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"plural","gloss":"复数","context":"On the wall, chalk showed how a noun could take a plural ending and how a pronoun could replace it.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"shorthand","gloss":"速记","context":"A learner who had once used shorthand at work submitted a handwritten manuscript about her experiences.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"specimen","gloss":"示例","context":"Their agenda included a visit to a municipal office, where a specimen application helped them prepare their own forms.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"chalk","gloss":"粉笔","context":"On the wall, chalk showed how a noun could take a plural ending and how a pronoun could replace it.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"handbook","gloss":"手册","context":"Learners used a directory to locate services and an index to find information in a handbook.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"paradigm","gloss":"范式","context":"By the final meeting, the center had adopted a different paradigm of achievement.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"The academy opened its evening doors to adults who had left secondary education early. Its dean refused to describe an illiterate learner as a failure. Many participants had worked since childhood or cared for relatives, and an unfamiliar alphabet could be as difficult as a university thesis. The first session therefore began with practical goals: reading a medicine label, writing an address, or understanding a child's nursery notice. A certificate would eventually recognize progress, but the semester was designed around everyday confidence rather than the collection of another credential.","zh":"这所学院在夜间为早早离开中学教育的成年人开放。院长拒绝把不会读写的学习者称为失败者。许多学员从小工作或照顾亲人，陌生的字母表对他们而言可能像大学论文一样困难。因此，第一次课从实用目标开始：读药品标签、写地址、看懂孩子托儿班的通知。将来的证书会认可他们的进步，但这一学期围绕日常生活的信心展开，而不是再获得一项资格。"},{"en":"A volunteer mentor gave each learner a notebook, a pen, and a pencil. On the wall, chalk showed how a noun could take a plural ending and how a pronoun could replace it. The group compared a singular verb with its changed form, then joined ideas using a conjunction. Instead of memorizing an isolated clause, they wrote messages they actually wanted to send. Handwriting was assessed for readability, not elegance. A brief oral discussion allowed participants to explain what they meant before turning the thought into a written sentence, making the page less intimidating.","zh":"志愿导师给每位学员一本笔记本、一支钢笔和一支铅笔。墙上用粉笔展示名词如何变成复数，以及代词如何替代名词。大家比较单数动词和变化后的形式，再用连词连接想法。他们不孤立地背诵从句，而是书写自己真正想发送的信息。书写的评价标准是能否读懂，而不是是否漂亮。简短的口头讨论让学员先说明意思，再写成句子，使纸页不再令人畏惧。"},{"en":"Materials came from the neighborhood rather than a remote academic catalog. A kindergarten brochure, a health pamphlet, and a library leaflet supplied genuine reading practice. Learners used a directory to locate services and an index to find information in a handbook. A paperback story introduced the pleasure of reading beyond necessity. Its preface explained why the author had chosen simple language. An editorial in a local newspaper became the subject of a seminar, while a short column prompted debate about bus fares. A junior volunteer prepared a summary so that everyone could return to the main points.","zh":"教材来自社区，而不是遥远的学术目录。幼儿园介绍册、健康小册子和图书馆传单提供真实阅读练习。学员利用名录查找服务，用索引在手册中寻找信息。平装故事书让他们体会到阅读不仅出于需要，也可以带来快乐。前言解释了作者为何使用简单语言。地方报纸社论成为讨论课的主题，短专栏则引发公交票价的争论。年轻志愿者准备了摘要，让大家能重新把握要点。"},{"en":"The curriculum included arithmetic and a little sociology: participants investigated why some families could access education more easily than others. Their agenda included a visit to a municipal office, where a specimen application helped them prepare their own forms. A learner who had once used shorthand at work submitted a handwritten manuscript about her experiences. Another compiled a dictionary of unfamiliar workplace terms. A quiz identified what needed more practice, but no diploma promise replaced careful feedback. Teachers treated each difficulty as information about instruction rather than evidence that the learner lacked ability.","zh":"课程包含算术和一点社会学：学员调查为什么一些家庭更容易获得教育机会。日程包括参观市政办公室，在那里申请表示例帮助他们填写自己的表格。一位曾在工作中使用速记的学员提交了亲手书写的经历稿，另一位整理了不熟悉的工作用语词典。小测验指出哪些内容需要更多练习，但承诺文凭不能取代认真反馈。教师把每个困难视为改进教学的信息，而不是学习者缺乏能力的证据。"},{"en":"By the final meeting, the center had adopted a different paradigm of achievement. One participant proudly read a school letter without asking a neighbor for help; another explained a tenancy agreement to a friend. Such changes were small enough to escape official statistics, yet large enough to alter relationships. Independence did not mean learning entirely alone. It meant knowing where to find assistance and having the confidence to judge it. The academy's most important result was therefore not a row of matching qualifications, but a community in which asking a question no longer carried shame.","zh":"最后一次聚会时，中心已经采用了不同的成就观。一位学员自豪地独立读懂学校来信，无须请邻居帮忙；另一位向朋友解释租赁合同。这些改变小到官方统计可能忽略，却大到足以改变人际关系。独立并不意味着完全独自学习，而是知道去哪里求助，并有信心判断帮助是否合适。因此，学院最重要的成果不是一排相同的资格证书，而是一个提问不再令人羞愧的共同体。"}],"previous":75,"next":77});
